    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Scum_and_Villainy\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy\">Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy</a></i> </p><p>An Ion Charger encases a Melee Weapon in a light <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ion\">Ion</a> field that flares to full strength anytime the Weapon strikes something. This causes the Melee Weapon to deal 2d6 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ion\">Ion</a> damage in addition to its normal Melee Damage. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feats\" title=\"Feats\">Feats</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Talents\" title=\"Talents\">Talents</a> that add to a Weapon's damage (such as the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Rapid_Strike\" title=\"Rapid Strike\">Rapid Strike</a> Feat) have no effect on the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ion\">Ion</a> damage dealt by a Weapon with an Ion Charger (though they increase the Weapon's base damage as normal). </p><p>Ion Chargers are common on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vibroblade\" title=\"Vibroblade\">Vibroblades</a>, and are often referred to as an \"Ionite Edge.\" </p>",
